Subject: auto-scroll follows the viewport, not only the content

What: createAutoScroll observes the scroller as well as its content, skips hidden
retained surfaces (`enabled`), lets a caller veto following for growth the reader
can already see (`mayFollow`), ends the settle window on the reader's click, and
restores follow intent on a remounted scroller (`restoreFollowing`).
Why: when the viewport grew and shrank back (the prompt dock losing and regaining a
status line as a turn completes) the clamped scrollTop was stranded one line short
of the bottom with no content resize to re-pin it.

